O:23:"PHPStan\Cache\CacheItem":2:{s:11:"variableKey";s:83:"v3-6.73.0.6-8.3.35-bf4375ef974923a376229528ed4f5ace2e8277309e9c755661b062ea2d138ec6";s:4:"data";a:22:{s:13:"locatedSource";a:2:{s:5:"class";s:60:"PHPStan\BetterReflection\SourceLocator\Located\LocatedSource";s:4:"data";a:2:{s:4:"name";s:42:"App\Modules\Inventory\Services\ExpiryWatch";s:8:"filename";s:77:"C:/xampp/htdocs/industrial_crm/app/Modules/Inventory/Services/ExpiryWatch.php";}}s:9:"namespace";s:30:"App\Modules\Inventory\Services";s:4:"name";s:42:"App\Modules\Inventory\Services\ExpiryWatch";s:9:"shortName";s:11:"ExpiryWatch";s:11:"isInterface";b:0;s:7:"isTrait";b:0;s:6:"isEnum";b:0;s:12:"isBackedEnum";b:0;s:9:"modifiers";i:32;s:10:"docComment";s:687:"/**
 * What the scheduler does about expiry, every day for every company:
 *
 *  - **Expire**: a batch past its expiry date that still has stock is marked *expired* — from then on it cannot be issued or moved, only scrapped.
 *  - **Warn**: a batch with stock that expires within `inventory.expiry_warning_days` (30 by default; 0 = off) tells the people who hold
 *    `stock.view`, once. The warning is *claimed* with one conditional UPDATE (`WHERE expiry_alerted_at IS NULL`) before anyone is told, so
 *    overlapping or repeated runs never send it twice.
 *
 * A batch with nothing left is ignored. (Raising a loss incident from an expired batch arrives with the loss module.)
